    "Practical part: the candidate's own machine with JDK 25, Apache Maven 3.9 or later and an IDE, plus the provided assessment project; the project runs fully offline after its one-time dependency setup, uses only an embedded in-memory H2 database, and needs no cloud account, container engine, AI service or shared hosted service."
  ],
  "instructions": "Spring Boot graded course-final practical (Part 1 of the Spring Boot course final, day S13), distinct from all practice. It is platform-scheduled as its own timed sitting outside the frozen day templates; S13 only names where the course closes. A 150-minute practical: one coherent candidate-local Spring Boot 4.1.2 project (pulled to the candidate's machine like the module labs, graded by the platform owner against the submitted project) of about 8 linked tasks across layers, persistence, validation and errors, testing, the outbound client and security, checked locally with mvn -q -o test. It draws only on taught course content and is varied or modestly harder than the practice labs and mastery checks: same skills, fresh scenario and data, no reused practice items. The pass mark is 70%. The graded multiple-choice part is the separate assessment spring-boot-final-mcq (30 questions, 30 minutes). Any weighting that combines the two parts into one overall result is set by the platform assessment owner. This blueprint is deliberately value-free: it carries no items and no answer material, and the practical project, hidden tests and scoring materials are held by the platform assessment owner and never enter this repository. Manual upload ownership is unchanged."
